ASoC: simple-card: name a link from the DT

The PCM a simple-card link creates is named "<cpu dai>-<codec dai>", which
means nothing to a user. Take the name from an optional link-name property
on the link node (or simple-audio-card,link-name on the card node for a
single link), so a board can name its outputs in the device tree, and pass
the name as an argument rather than as the format string.

--- a/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c	2026-11-03 14:37:11
+++ b/sound/soc/generic/simple-card.c	2026-11-03 14:37:11
@@ -186,6 +186,8 @@
 	enum snd_soc_trigger_order trigger_start = SND_SOC_TRIGGER_ORDER_DEFAULT;
 	enum snd_soc_trigger_order trigger_stop  = SND_SOC_TRIGGER_ORDER_DEFAULT;
 	bool playback_only = 0, capture_only = 0;
+	const char *link_name = NULL;
+	char prop[128];
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = simple_util_parse_daifmt(dev, node, codec,
@@ -221,7 +223,11 @@
 	dai_link->init			= simple_util_dai_init;
 	dai_link->ops			= &simple_ops;
 
-	ret = simple_util_set_dailink_name(priv, dai_link, name);
+	snprintf(prop, sizeof(prop), "%slink-name", prefix);
+	of_property_read_string(node, prop, &link_name);
+
+	ret = simple_util_set_dailink_name(priv, dai_link, "%s",
+					   link_name ?: name);
 end:
 	return simple_ret(priv, ret);
 }
